---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import EmailReveal from '../../components/EmailReveal.astro';
import { legal } from '../../config/legal';
import { site } from '../../config/site';
import { link } from '../../lib/url';

const toc = [
  { id: 'about', title: 'About these terms' },
  { id: 'using', title: 'Using this website' },
  { id: 'misuse', title: 'What you must not do' },
  { id: 'information', title: 'Information on this website' },
  { id: 'ip', title: 'Intellectual property' },
  { id: 'links', title: 'Links to other websites' },
  { id: 'availability', title: 'Availability and changes' },
  { id: 'liability', title: 'Our responsibility to you' },
  { id: 'law', title: 'Governing law' },
  { id: 'changes', title: 'Changes to these terms' },
  { id: 'contact', title: 'Contact' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  doc="terms"
  description="The terms for using the APOLLO Network website: permitted use, what is not allowed, intellectual property and our responsibilities."
  lead="Plain terms for using this website. They cover the site itself — not services, which are always agreed separately in writing."
  toc={toc}
  summary={[
    'You are welcome to read, share links to and learn from this website.',
    'Please do not attack, overload or misuse it, or copy its content or design for your own use.',
    'The site is information, not an offer: any work is agreed separately in writing.',
    'Nothing here affects your legal rights as a consumer.',
  ]}
>
  <section id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <h2 id="about-title">About these terms</h2>
    <p>
      These terms apply to your use of the {site.name} website. {legal.operator} is{' '}
      {legal.operatorDescription} operated from {legal.location}; “we” and “us” refer to it. By
      using the website you accept these terms. If you do not agree with them, please do not use the
      site.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our <a href={link('privacy/')}>Privacy Policy</a> and{' '}
      <a href={link('cookies/')}>Cookie Policy</a> explain how personal data and device storage are
      handled.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="using" aria-labelledby="using-title">
    <h2 id="using-title">Using this website</h2>
    <p>
      The website is free to use. You may browse it, read and save pages for your own reference, and
      share links to it. It is intended for people and businesses who want to learn about APOLLO
      Network and its work.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="misuse" aria-labelledby="misuse-title">
    <h2 id="misuse-title">What you must not do</h2>
    <p>When using this website or the ways of contacting us from it, you must not:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>use it for anything unlawful, fraudulent or harmful;</li>
      <li>try to gain unauthorised access to it, or to any system or account connected with it;</li>
      <li>
        disrupt, overload or impair it — for example with automated traffic, denial-of-service
        attacks or malicious code;
      </li>
      <li>
        copy, republish or reuse substantial parts of its content, design or graphics without our
        written permission;
      </li>
      <li>suggest that you are, or are endorsed by, APOLLO Network when you are not;</li>
      <li>use our enquiry channels to send spam, abuse or unlawful material.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Good-faith security research that follows our <a href={link('security/')}>security policy</a>{' '}
      is welcome and is not treated as misuse.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="information" aria-labelledby="information-title">
    <h2 id="information-title">Information on this website</h2>
    <p>
      The content is general information about APOLLO Network and its work. It is not professional,
      legal, financial or technical advice for your situation, and while we aim to keep it accurate,
      we do not promise that it is complete or up to date.
    </p>
    <p>
      Descriptions of services are an invitation to get in touch, not an offer. No products,
      subscriptions or services are sold through this website: any work is agreed separately, in
      writing, with its own terms.
    </p>
    <p>
      The APOLLO Network Application is described as it currently stands. It is in private
      development and not publicly available, and its features and plans may change.
    </p>
    <p>
      The APOLLO assistant gives short, pre-written answers to common questions. It is not an AI,
      and its answers are general guidance only.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="ip" aria-labelledby="ip-title">
    <h2 id="ip-title">Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      Unless stated otherwise, the APOLLO Network name and branding, the design of this website, its
      original graphics and visual effects, its written content, and its demonstrations belong to
      APOLLO Network. All rights are reserved.
    </p>
    <p>
      The website’s source code is publicly viewable on{' '}
      <a href={site.repository} rel="noopener noreferrer external">
        GitHub<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens external site)</span>
      </a>
      , but it is <strong>not open source</strong>. Being able to see the code does not grant a
      licence to use, copy, modify or distribute it, beyond what GitHub’s own terms allow for
      viewing public repositories on GitHub.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some material belongs to others and is used under their licences — for example the{' '}
      <a href={link('licenses/inter-OFL.txt')}>Inter</a> and{' '}
      <a href={link('licenses/space-grotesk-OFL.txt')}>Space Grotesk</a> typefaces, available under
      the SIL Open Font License. Names and marks of other companies, such as GitHub and Google,
      belong to their owners.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="links" aria-labelledby="links-title">
    <h2 id="links-title">Links to other websites</h2>
    <p>
      Links to other websites are provided for convenience. We do not control those sites and are
      not responsible for their content, availability or policies.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="availability" aria-labelledby="availability-title">
    <h2 id="availability-title">Availability and changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may change, suspend or withdraw any part of the website at any time. We aim to keep it
      available and working well, but cannot guarantee that it will always be available,
      uninterrupted or free of errors.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="liability" aria-labelledby="liability-title">
    <h2 id="liability-title">Our responsibility to you</h2>
    <p>
      The website is provided free of charge, as information. To the extent the law allows, we are
      not responsible for loss or damage arising from your use of the website or from relying on its
      content.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing in these terms excludes or limits our liability for death or personal injury caused by
      negligence, for fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation, or for anything else that cannot be
      excluded or limited by law. If you are a consumer, these terms do not affect your statutory
      rights.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="law" aria-labelledby="law-title">
    <h2 id="law-title">Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the law of {legal.governingLaw}, and the courts of{' '}
      {legal.governingLaw} have jurisdiction. If you are a consumer living elsewhere in the United
      Kingdom, you may also bring proceedings in the courts where you live.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes" aria-labelledby="changes-title">
    <h2 id="changes-title">Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms. The “last updated” date at the top shows when they last changed,
      and the version on this page is the one that applies.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
    <h2 id="contact-title">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms: <EmailReveal /> or use the{' '}
      <a href={link('contact/')}>contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
